            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Persian for to get vaccinated, then the Persian for a check-up."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: عیادت کردن",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "عیادت کردن ('iyâdat kardan) — \"to visit (a sick person)\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "همکارانش در بیمارستان از او عیادت کردند. hamkârânash dar bimârestân az u 'iyâdat kardand. His colleagues visited him in hospital."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "az kasi 'iyâdat kardan: said only of visiting the sick. 'iyâdat + kardan."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "'iyâdat is a loan, usually traced to Arabic ʿiyāda, 'visiting the sick'. EtymDB has no entry for it. kardan is inherited Persian."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
