          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "پرستاری کردن (parastâri kardan) — \"to nurse, to care for\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "وقتی بیمار بودم، خواهرم از من پرستاری کرد. vaqti bimâr budam, khâharam az man parastâri kard. When I was ill, my sister nursed me."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "parastâr 'nurse' + -i + kardan. The person nursed takes az."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "parastâri is built on parastâr, 'nurse', which is inherited: EtymDB traces it to a Middle Persian word for a maidservant (EtymDB). The ending -i and kardan are native too."
            }
          ]
        },
